e":"Transfer to a new artwork or performance"}],"title":"Year 4, Week 12, Lesson 2: Character scenes","unit_number":3,"unit_title":"Improvisation and playbuilding","week":12,"week_in_unit":2,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\nExample: Circumstances: lost property room after lunch. Beat 1: two students search. Beat 2: one finds a diary and hesitates. Reaction: the owner enters and both freeze, then negotiate kindly.\n\nWrite what makes this example effective, naming the element, technique or performance choice and its effect.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"Scene building blocks.","caption":"Plan the change.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Circumstances</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">who where when</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Beat</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">action shift</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Reactions drive drama.","caption":"Respond and change.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Reaction</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">change after hearing</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Short lines</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">playable talk</text></g></svg>"}],"year_level":"Year 4"}') WHERE seed_key='s2-arts-y4-w12-l2' AND family_id IS NULL;
